  "notes": [
    "Slot rectangles trace HP's 'Figure 6 - Loading order for dual CPU configurations' diagram, so the POSITIONS are accurate to that figure.",
    "The circled numbers in the figure are population order, not silkscreen slot names. The 'label' fields below give the population-order number.",
    "CPU assignment is certain: odd population orders are CPU0, even are CPU1, which the figure confirms directly.",
    "Channel-pairing is well supported: HP fills one DIMM per channel (orders 1-8) before the second (orders 9-16), so order N and N+8 share a channel - and every pair that predicts does sit adjacent in the same physical bank on the figure.",
    "Which pair is lettered A vs B vs C vs D is INFERRED from 'first populated channel is A'. Nothing in SMBIOS confirms it. If HP letters them differently the CPU is still right but the channel letter may rotate within that CPU.",
    "Verify by pulling one stick, noting which serial disappears from `sudo dmidecode -t 17`, and seeing which key stops reporting."
  ],

